"""The A2A agent card's skills (generated by genproj).

The card is owned by the container: it is declared here and re-registered with
the LiteLLM gateway on startup, so a changed skill or description ships with the
image instead of drifting in a UI. Describe the domain honestly - LiteLLM's
agent registry matches a task against the card's name, description and skills by
semantic similarity, so a placeholder description is how a router fails to find
the agent.

The skills are plain dictionaries, not SDK objects, because they are used twice:
`agent/main.py` builds the served `a2a.types.AgentCard` from them, and
`agent/register.py` sends the same list to LiteLLM as JSON. A dict literal is
both a valid `AgentSkill(**skill)` argument and JSON-serialisable, so the served
card and the registered card cannot drift.

The name, description and protocol version come from agent/main.py and the
capability configuration; this file owns only the skills.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

AGENT_SKILLS: list[dict] = {{agentSkillsLiteral}}
